      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As for the last two examples, I\u0027m not sure those strings are supposed to be caught by the UnnecessaryCheckNotNull checker you pointed to, because it explicitly mentions checking for a literal in the first argument - a String being passed around should be considered a valid non-null value.\n\nI\u0027m not saying the implementation is wrong. What I mean is the check itself is not useful.",
