      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t that a bit unfair? It\u0027s after all exceedingly rare that the error message isn\u0027t a literal. Or a string concatenation expression - if the checker doesn\u0027t handle that either I would agree its usefulness (in this particular regard) is a bit more limited, but still far from useless.\n\nYour 2nd and 3rd examples are really disappointing, though.",
